# tab_constructions

**Claim carried:** C5: whether the interval construction changes width and coverage, for every estimator including PPI++.

**Shows:** E5: per dataset, n and method, mean width (empirical coverage %) under each interval construction (columns are the constructions that were run, named as in cells.csv: wald = normal quantile, t, wilson, wald_trunc = Wald clipped to [0, 1], boot_t = studentised bootstrap, run only for the pooled linear and isotonic-calibrated estimators, cp = Clopper-Pearson, labels only; a column appears only if a cell has it and -- = not run for that estimator); dagger = coverage fails the win rule. Longtable.

**How to read:** read across a row: same estimator, same draws, different construction; compare the daggers of one row to see whether any construction brings coverage to the pre-fixed rule. At small n the reference (PPI++) is itself daggered, so a dagger there is not specific to one method.

